<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Thanjavur Nayak kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1532 CE – 1673 CE · capital Thanjavur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Nayaka kingdom of the Kaveri delta whose rulers made Thanjavur a centre of Carnatic music, painting and Telugu literature.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sevappa-nayak">Sevappa Nayak</a>, a <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara</a> noble married into the royal family, was appointed to govern the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> region around 1532. His dynasty ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>-rich Kaveri delta as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> and, after its decline, as independent kings.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raghunatha-nayak">Raghunatha Nayak</a>, the most celebrated ruler, was a poet, musician and patron who supported <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara</a> in its last wars. The court produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telugu-language">Telugu</a> yakshagana dramas and musical treatises, laying foundations of Carnatic music. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaks</a> permitted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danish-east-india-company">Danish East India Company</a> to settle at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/danish-india">Tranquebar</a> in 1620. Temples at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumbakonam">Kumbakonam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> were enlarged.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Conflict with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madurai-nayak-dynasty">Madurai Nayak dynasty</a> led to the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayaraghava-nayak">Vijayaraghava Nayak</a> in 1673. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bijapur-sultanate">Bijapur Sultanate</a> then sent the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ekoji-i">Ekoji</a>, who seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> in 1675 and founded the Maratha line of Thanjavur.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/thanjavur-nayak-kingdom.jpg" alt="Thanjavur Nayak kingdom" width="250" height="273"><figcaption>Image: Southernstar · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanjore_Nayak_Kingdom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1532 CE – 1673 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Thanjavur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sevappa Nayak, Raghunatha Nayak, Vijayaraghava Nayak</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Telugu, Tamil</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Thanjavur Nayaks, Nayaks of Tanjore</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1602&amp;focus=thanjavur-nayak-kingdom" aria-label="Thanjavur Nayak kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6860 1775 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Thanjavur Nayak kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7180 2031L7088 1864M7180 2031L7154 2063M7180 2031L7180 2031"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7088 1864h0M7154 2063h0M7180 2031h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7180 2031h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7180 2031h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Thanjavur. <a href="/atlas?year=1602&amp;focus=thanjavur-nayak-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
